Subject: [PATCH] mmc: a larger read-ahead for SD cards

Every block device starts with a read-ahead of 128 KB. With it a microSD card in
this tablet reads at about 40 MB/s, from the filesystem or the raw device alike,
while its bus runs UHS SDR104 at 160 MHz, some 80 MB/s. With 512 KB the same
card reads at 68 MB/s; with 2048 KB no faster. Stock left it at 128 KB too.

Only SD cards get it. The eMMC holds the system and the apps, which Android
reads in small scattered pieces, page faults on mapped code included, and the
read-ahead applies to those as well: there a larger one only reads more of what
is not needed and fills memory with it. Userspace can still change either value
through /sys/block/*/queue/read_ahead_kb.
---
--- drivers/mmc/card/queue.c
+++ drivers/mmc/card/queue.c
@@ -413,6 +413,15 @@
 	if (!mq->queue)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/*
+	 * An SD card mostly holds large files, read from start to end, and the
+	 * default read-ahead of 128 KB left one at half the bus' speed. The eMMC
+	 * keeps the default: Android reads it in small, scattered pieces, and a
+	 * larger read-ahead there would only fill memory with pages nobody asked for.
+	 */
+	if (mmc_card_sd(card))
+		mq->queue->backing_dev_info.ra_pages = (512 * 1024) / PAGE_CACHE_SIZE;
+
 	if ((host->caps2 & MMC_CAP2_STOP_REQUEST) &&
 			host->ops->stop_request &&
 			mq->card->ext_csd.hpi_en)
